    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>I got what I needed from this answer: <a href=3D"https://stackoverflow.c=
om/a/41613532/1223975">https://stackoverflow.com/a/41613532/1223975</a></p>

<p>..turns out using <code>wait &lt;pid&gt;</code> <em>will only work if th=
at pid is a child process of the current process</em>.</p>

<p>However the following will work for any process:</p>

<h3>To wait for any process to finish</h3>

<p>Linux:</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">tail</span> --pid=3D<=
span class=3D"hljs-variable">$pid</span> -f /dev/null
</code></pre>

<p>Darwin (requires that <code>$pid</code> has open files):</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">lsof -p <span class=3D"hljs-variable">$pid</span> +=
r 1 &amp;&gt;/dev/null
</code></pre>

<h3>With timeout (seconds)</h3>

<p>Linux:</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">timeout</span> <span =
class=3D"hljs-variable">$timeout</span> <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">tail<=
/span> --pid=3D<span class=3D"hljs-variable">$pid</span> -f /dev/null
</code></pre>

<p>Darwin (requires that <code>$pid</code> has open files):</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">lsof -p <span class=3D"hljs-variable">$pid</span> +=
r 1m%s -t | grep -qm1 $(<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">date</span> -v+<span =
class=3D"hljs-variable">${timeout}</span>S +%s 2&gt;/dev/null || <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-built_in">echo</span> INF)
</code></pre>
    </div>
