    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>If you need to wait for a process by its name:</p>
<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">pidwait firefox
</code></pre>
<p>This will wait for the process "firefox" to finish. <code>pidwait</code>=
 is likely already installed on your system. It's part of the <code>pkill</=
code>/<code>pgrep</code>/<code>pidwait</code> bundle, packaged as <code>pro=
cps-ng</code> package on ArchLinux, installed by default on ArchLinux and D=
ebian.</p>
    </div>
